n Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6dd26caa40bc8fff3fdfa6bb846a5ffdac481a47.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6dd26caa40bc8fff3fdfa6bb846a5ffdac481a47.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 24 at 3:31PM MDT until October 25 at 3:30PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Northwestern Archuleta County in southwestern Colorado...\nSouthwestern Hinsdale County in southwestern Colorado...\nLa Plata County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 330 PM MDT Sunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Numerous roads\nremain closed due to flooding. Low-water crossings are inundated\nwith water and may not be passable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 329 PM MDT, local law enforcement reported heavy rain in the\nwarned area due to thunderstorms. Flooding is ongoing Between 2\nand 4 inches of rain have fallen since Thursday morning.\n- Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are possible in the\nwarned area. This could cause additional rises within rivers,\ncreeks and streams.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDurango, Bayfield, Ignacio, La Plata, Falfa, Oxford, Bondad,\nHesperus, Breen, Vallecito, Mayday, Kline, Marvel, Tiffany,\nAllison and Redmesa.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-25T15:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a78d65db70a62b4ca86f2ab0f3dbfe4836abe983.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a78d65db70a62b4ca86f2ab0f3dbfe4836abe983.001.1"}],"afd":{"off